73900c11e8dc999f8cbde7ba","commit_subject":"Add a timeout to the PTDE sampler:   - ptde.py/run.py: add a user-settable per-call wall-clock timeout     (sampler.eval_timeout, default: None — no timeout) to the PTDE     sampler.   - A logp call that exceeds this timeout is rejected and     its full raw and physical parameter set are logged for offline     reproduction.   - The worker pool is recycled after rejection   - It should be understood that this is a workaround for an unhandled     pathological case in the backend model computation and we are     imposing a poorly-understood, a priori bias against such pathological     cases with unquantified bounds.   - The intent is that this feature would be used as a bridge to help     diagnose and fix such pathological cases. It would be faster and     more scientifically sound to avoid pathological regions with     explicit priors or properly handle them within the logp call.   - examples/DC2018_128/DC2018_128.yaml opts in with eval_timeout: 10,     since we are seeing long VBMicrolensing calls (likely at extreme     values of s & q) and we are trying to understand them","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"neomjs/neo","commit_timestamp":"2026-07-04T03:03:46Z","branch":"dev","commit_sha":"cd34583d8bba20489762ad63894e601956e2930e","github_link":"https://github.com/neomjs/neo/commit/cd34583d8bba20489762ad63894e601956e2930e","commit_subject":"feat(fleetmanager): cockpit design tokens + verification surface (#14578) (#14622)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"neomjs/neo","commit_timestamp":"2026-07-04T03:03:19Z","branch":"dev","commit_sha":"9b8fa16cf09b425e348af28d456b171b1c1592bd","github_link":"https://github.com/neomjs/neo/commit/9b8fa16cf09b425e348af28d456b171b1c1592bd","commit_subject":"feat(fleet): runtime-status wire method — fleetRuntimeStatus (#14595) (#14602)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"moq-dev/moq","commit_timestamp":"2026-07-04T03:03:01Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"0f4166d288e9059c1757009358c91a1cd62959d6"